From a7e7a2bf887332fba51b680df20f40bab7f59e50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:12:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat: set the scale from the gap by voice; switch models
 with cycle_model once one stands in the gap; tight fits

- "the opening is 34 and a half inches tall" / "the gap is 24 inches wide" -> scale_gap {component_id,
  axis, real_m}: the headset sets its scale from its own tape of the gap (the kitchen scan reads
  ~1.47x small indoors). The rest of the same reply ("... and find a dishwasher that fits") uses the
  corrected size. "34 and a half" is one amount, not two phrases.
- "next / previous one", "option N" with a model already in the gap -> cycle_model {index, part_id}:
  the app's placement editor swaps it where it stands (its adjusted pose, one undo step). The first
  "put it in there" (or "option N" into an empty gap) stays place_part.
- place_part fits: "tight" when at most 5 mm over on one axis (amber on the headset), and the spoken
  line says so ("It's tight: 3 millimetres too wide.").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
